# TS3: ARM A (the control) of the ABAB for the sampler lever(s).
# TIMED ARM of the paired timing ABAB on coding prompts (audits OFF). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission
# order: A = c2-packed-tp4-best-strace (the control: the all-levers recipe with hang fix A), B = c2-packed-tp4-best-samp (the control plus EXACTLY QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX=1).
# The tests: warmup, coding (one stream), concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k, the padded-4k shape) and concurrent4_code_32k (four real-code prompts
# of 32k, the long-context shape). 800 tokens out each, started together. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache (30 the first
# time a profile compiles); the four tests 15-35 min: 30-60 min.
# Read: the [PACKED-PHASE] lines (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and the [PACKED-PUBLISH] medians at 4 live in each concurrent test:
# the round wall, the per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean. Judge the arms PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run
# (a busy host skews host phases 10-20%) and repeat before believing a small gap.
# Lever S1 (QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX): the per-shard argmax of every verify is one scan launch on 110 cores plus a one-core fold instead of untilize + ArgMax + the V4a gather (about
# 1.8 ms of a 59 ms verify). Read the verify trace_ms and readback_ms at live=4, paired per round; the served text must equal the control's (the ids are exactly
# the control's), so compare the accepted prefixes with speed_window_compare (exit 0) as well.
# The smoke check fails the run on a fall-back line or on no engaged line for the lever(s) of this arm. A hang on a timed arm is a finding; both arms carry hang
# fix A (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE) and the tail caps, as production does. OPTIONAL: the numbers are the product.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/samp-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/samp-draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-samp-1 is the image B0 builds from the pushed tp4/samp-draft commit while production serves (it carries
# tp4_shard_argmax, tp4_draft_conv and tp4_draft_heads and their kernels, which are new); a later commit needs a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-samp-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
